    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="3db637d3-5fe4-5aee-a632-7af27b70782b" activityNameId="47cbd179-3381-5fd3-a6ef-cdd5aeef273e" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xxx Polylactide, granulate, NatureWorks Nebraska</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xxx Polylactide, granulate, NatureWorks Nebraska
Inventory refers to the production of 1 kg  PLA in the world largest PLA plant. The inventories include the LCI data from the report of the producer NatureWorks. ;
UUID: fba31eaa-9310-3098-86ba-1732d42311f5
The publication contains only cumulative results. To get more transparency and to be in accordance with other ecoi nvent processes and the guideline the data has been splitted up in maize production, enegy use, transport and waste water treatement. The infrastructure has been added. So the emissions from energy consumption, waste water treatement and raw material inputs have been subtracted resulting in a difference in NMVOC emissions.shown in this process.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Evaluation of plant site in Minnetonka
Time period: undefined
Production volume:  
Sampling: Data were compiled from LCI report of producer 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_fba31eaa-9310-3098-86ba-1732d42311f5.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
